HLstatsX Community Edition
Heatmap Generation Installation Instructions

WARNING: Heatmap generation will consume alot of processor time.  Please be sure to plan accordingly!
300k kills on one map will take ~10min to generate on one 2.4Ghz core processor.

Install:
	- set DB_HOST, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD and DB_NAME in the .env file at the
	  repository root (the same file the web pages use, see .env.example), or as
	  environment variables. HEATMAP_WEB_PATH sets the web folder the images are
	  written to (default: the web folder of this checkout).
	- put one overview image per map in src/<game>/<map>.jpg (see below).

To generate heatmaps:
	- run: php generate.php
	  (--game=<code> and --map=<name> limit the run, --disable-cache starts again
	  from scratch, --ignore-infected skips L4D infected deaths)

Output: <web>/hlstatsimg/games/<game code>/heatmaps/<map>-kill.jpg and
<map>-kill-thumb.jpg, shown on the map page.


Source images
-------------

The "HeatmapPack" of ready-made images (once downloaded from hlxce.com / the
HLX-Extras repository) is no longer available anywhere. Each map needs a JPEG
of its overview (radar) image:

	src/<game>/<map>.jpg

<game> is the "game" column of hlstats_Heatmap_Config (the realgame, e.g. css,
cstrike, tf), <map> the map name. Only letters, digits, "_", "-", "!", "+" and "."
are accepted in both.

How kill positions are placed on the image (hlstats_Heatmap_Config):

	pixel_x = (pos_x + xoffset) / scale
	pixel_y = (pos_y + yoffset) / scale     (pos_y is negated first when flipy = 1,
	                                         pos_x when flipx = 1)

rotate = 1 swaps x and y. The shipped rows match the images of the old pack:
an image made another way needs its own values.

For Source games, the overview the game itself uses is the easiest source:
	- the image: materials/overviews/<map>_radar.vtf (or .dds), converted to JPEG
	  at its original size (usually 1024x1024) with any VTF tool;
	- the position: resource/overviews/<map>.txt has "pos_x", "pos_y" and
	  "scale" for that image. Set
		xoffset = -pos_x
		yoffset = pos_y
		scale   = scale
		flipx = 0, flipy = 1, rotate = 0 (try rotate = 1 if that file has "rotate" "1")

	  UPDATE hlstats_Heatmap_Config SET xoffset = ..., yoffset = ..., scale = ...,
	         flipx = 0, flipy = 1, rotate = 0
	  WHERE game = '<game>' AND map = '<map>';

A map with no row in hlstats_Heatmap_Config is not generated: insert one with
the same columns.

Other columns: days (how far back kills are read), brush (small or large),
font (HUD text size), thumbw/thumbh (thumbnail size as a fraction of the image),
cropx1/cropy1/cropx2/cropy2 (crop before saving, 0 = none).

report problems to the issue tracker of this repository
